  "about": "The epistola of the formulary “Commemoration of All the Faithful Departed — Mass I” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "Brethren: Behold, I tell you a mystery: All of us will indeed rise again, but not all of us will be changed. In an instant, in the blink of an eye, at the final trumpet — for the trumpet will ring out, and the dead will rise again incorrupt, and we will be changed, since this corruptible must put on incorruption, and this mortal must put on immortality. And when this mortal has put on immortality, the saying that is written will then be fulfilled: Death is swallowed up in victory. Where, O death, is your victory? Where, O death, is your sting? And the sting of death is sin, while sin’s strength is the law. But to God be thanks, who gave us victory through our Lord Jesus Christ.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w006", "w007", "w008"], "anchor": "w008", "gloss": "we will indeed all rise" }, { "words": ["w010", "w011", "w012"], "anchor": "w012", "gloss": "we will not all be changed" }, { "words": ["w021", "w022", "w023"], "anchor": "w021", "gloss": "for the trumpet will sound" }, { "words": ["w031", "w032"], "anchor": "w031", "gloss": "for it is necessary" }, { "words": ["w033", "w034"], "anchor": "w034", "gloss": "for this corruptible body" }, { "words": ["w038", "w039"], "anchor": "w039", "gloss": "for this mortal body" }, { "words": ["w042", "w043"], "anchor": "w042", "gloss": "but when" }, { "words": ["w044", "w045"], "anchor": "w045", "gloss": "this mortal body" }, { "words": ["w052", "w053"], "anchor": "w052", "gloss": "has been written" }, { "words": ["w054", "w055"], "anchor": "w054", "gloss": "has been swallowed up" }, { "words": ["w069", "w070"], "anchor": "w069", "gloss": "now the sting" }, { "words": ["w072", "w073"], "anchor": "w072", "gloss": "is sin" }, { "words": ["w074", "w075"], "anchor": "w074", "gloss": "and the power" }, { "words": ["w078", "w079", "w080"], "anchor": "w080", "gloss": "but thanks to God" }] }
  },
